<header class="flex items-center justify-between relative z-10 pt-5 lg:pt-0">
  <a href="/" class="flex items-center gap-2.5">
    {% if store.logoImageUrl %}
      {%- comment -%} Decorative: the link already carries the store name as text. {%- endcomment -%}
      <img
        src="{{ store.logoImageUrl | image_url: width: 64 }}"
        alt=""
        width="26"
        height="26"
        class="block size-6.5 shrink-0 rounded-full object-cover"
      >
    {% else %}
      {% render 'logo-placeholder', logo_size: 'size-6.5' %}
    {% endif %}
    <span class="font-medium text-white">{{ store.name }}</span>
  </a>
  <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
    <button
      type="button"
      data-cart-open
      aria-label="Cart"
      class="relative flex items-center justify-center size-9 rounded-xl bg-black/7.5 text-white/70 transition-colors cursor-pointer hover:bg-white/10 hover:text-white"
    >
      <img src="{{ 'cart.svg' | asset_url }}" alt="" width="16" height="16">
      {%- comment -%}
        The cart lives in the browser, so the page is rendered without it: the counter reads
        the cart itself and keeps up as it changes. An empty cart shows no badge.
      {%- endcomment %}
      <nz-cart-counter hidden-when-empty class="absolute -top-1.5 -right-1.5"></nz-cart-counter>
    </button>
    {%- comment -%}
      The page is cached for every visitor, so the link cannot depend on who is signed in. The
      orders page is the account: it sends a buyer who is not signed in to sign in, and back.
    {%- endcomment %}
    <a
      href="/orders"
      aria-label="Account"
      class="flex items-center justify-center size-9 rounded-xl bg-black/7.5 text-white/70 transition-colors hover:bg-white/10 hover:text-white"
    >
      <img src="{{ 'user.svg' | asset_url }}" alt="" width="16" height="16">
    </a>
  </div>
</header>
